Some of the cursed items have no penalty to being cursed other than being
non-removable, which often isn't much of a problem if the item is already
very useful. Here's a few ideas to change this:

cursed boots of kicking:
Randomly kicks items/monsters when next to them. This could be quite
frustrating in a long corridor - walk up to that scroll, kick it away,
walk up to it, kick it away again... As a slight advantage, makes this
otherwise difficult to identify item more obvious.

cursed boots of jumping:
Forces you to jump with every movement (legendary basis for this). This
makes movement very fast but awkward to control - think bishops only
moving on one set of squares on a chessboard. You could attempt to switch
onto the other set of squares by jumping into walls and things, causing
pain.

cursed helm of telepathy:
Amplifies mind flayer's telepathic attack.

cursed amulet of magical breathing:
Makes stinking cloud/gas traps more dangerous.

